{
  "title": "Spontaneous Osteonecrosis of the Knee (SONK)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3026/spontaneous-osteonecrosis-of-the-knee-sonk",
  "subtitle": "Updated: May 10 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Spontaneous osteonecrosis of the knee (SONK) is an idiopathic condition that leads to the development of a crescent shaped osteonecrosis lesion, mostly commonly in the epiphysis of the medial femoral condyle.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be radiographic for advanced disease but may require MRI in determining the extent of disease.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally nonoperative as most cases are self-limiting. Surgical management is indicated for progressive cases that fail conservative management.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common in **middle age and elderly**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "affects **females** (>55yo) more frequently than males",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "99% of patients have only **one joint involved**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "usually epiphysis of **medial femoral condyle**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may represent a subchondral insufficiency fracture",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "degenerative cascade involves posterior horn medial meniscal tears, which may involve the root attachment site",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "can occur post-arthroscopically",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "most commonly after partial meniscectomy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "thought to be related to altered joint biomechanics",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**sudden onset** of severe knee pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "effusion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "limited range of motion secondary to pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "tenderness over medial femoral condyle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3026/images/04109044-4c5a-40ca-9d40-87a7eda96ef0_sonk..jpg",
              "caption": "SONK of the medial femoral condyle"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "standing AP and lateral of hip, knee and ankle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3026/images/11a_moved.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most useful study",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "is helpful to confirm the diagnosis and assist in determining the extent of disease helping guide treatment considerations",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "lesion is crescent shaped",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Must differentiate from",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**osteochondritis dissecans**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "more common on lateral aspect of medial femoral condyle in adolescent males",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**transient osteoporosis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "more common in young to middle age men",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**bone bruises and occult fractures**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "associated trauma, bone fragility or overuse",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "NSAIDs, narcotics, protected weight bearing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "mainstay of treatment as most cases resolve",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "physical therapy directed at quadriceps strengthening",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "initial conservative measure and has shown good results",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "arthroplasty",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "when symptoms fail to respond to conservative treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "successful results reported with TKA (larger lesions or bone collapse) and UKA (smaller lesions) when properly indicated",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "high tibial osteotomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "when angular malalignment present",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
